  message: "PREMISE RE-CHECK 2026-09-29 on dev 6929699126: CURRENT, two facts drifted. Still no catalogue row for open or close in c.yaml or cpp.yaml (they appear only in ambiguous_names, c.yaml:19-20); nor openat/creat/fcntl/dup.\n\nA ROW WOULD MATCH: with a scratch --io-primitives overlay (fcntl.open fs_read, unistd.close fs_write), classify_call on qemu-dtc's real include slot (...,fcntl.h,unistd.h) classifies both, via #1291's slot split; a file without those headers is still refused. Base catalogue: open/close land in external_potential.\n\nDRIFT: (1) \"inert twice over\" is not exact: ambiguous_names membership still makes c.py stamp the include slot, and the calls surface as external_potential, not as nothing. (2) qemu-dtc (194ac94) has 4 open + 4 close call sites, not 6 + 5 -- the filed count included string literals (\"open(\\\"%s\\\")\", perror(\"open()\")).\n\nANALOGUES: of c's 19 ambiguous names only open, close, bind, listen have no row; bind/listen carry a dated removal decision (c.yaml:182, INV-nular/WI-dosov), open/close carry none. fclose is already fs_write (c.yaml:69) -- a precedent for close. In passing: cpp.yaml:8 says C++ inherits ::open from C, which is false while c.yaml has no row. Artifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_09292026/bulub/."  # d50c
