  clock: 4  # 4cbd
  nonce: 4cbd  # 4cbd
  message: "FIXED in PR #1294 (merged, dev 8a1f82137a). open/openat are fcntl rows under fs_read AND fs_write (stdio.fopen / Go os.OpenFile shape); io_boundary._MODE_ARGUMENT_POSITIONS[\"c\"] reads the OR-ed flag NAMES (O_WRONLY/O_RDWR/O_CREAT/O_TRUNC/O_APPEND -> w, O_RDONLY -> r); an unreadable flag keeps the first-declared fs_read row. creat is fs_write. close(2): NO ROW BY DECISION (2026-09-29) -- it moves no bytes, python's os.close precedent; fclose keeps fs_write because it flushes. fcntl admitted to CATALOGUE_SCOPE[\"c\"]. test_every_ambiguous_name_has_a_row_or_a_declared_refusal pins the rowless set {bind, listen, close}.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev: fixture f.c with open(p, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT, 0644) / open(p, O_RDONLY) / openat(d, p, O_RDWR) -> io-boundaries fs_write fcntl.open + fcntl.openat, fs_read fcntl.open (was external_potential). getenv -> open(p, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT) under host_secret -> host_fs: VIOLATED, stdlib.getenv -> fcntl.open. Control: a static project-local open() with no <fcntl.h> classifies nothing.\nA/B on 10 C repos (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bulub_09292026/RESULT.md): 159 open/openat/creat calls newly classify (crun 80, redis 28, passt 16); redis mode spot-check 6/6 correct; 0 verdicts changed; +37 taint flows at C's structural precision (2 read back were literal paths -- WI-himob's imprecision, not this row)."  # 4cbd
